# EdgeDB 3.0 | Gel Blog
created: 2023-06-22, last updated: 2026-06-16, [Read more](https://www.geldata.com/blog/edgedb-3-0)

```
type Person {
required name: str;
trigger log_update after update for each do (
insert AuditLog {
action := 'update',
target_name := __new__.name,
change := __old__.name ++ '->' ++ __new__.name
}
);
}
type AuditLog {
...
timestamp: datetime {
default := datetime_current();
}
target_name: str;
change: str;
}
...
```
type Post {
required title: str;
required body: str;
author: str;
byline: str {
# Cache computed byline on every update.
rewrite insert, update using (
'by ' ++
__subject__.author ++
' on ' ++
to_str(__subject__.created, 'Mon DD, YYYY')
)
}
}
```
...
In essence, the distinction between the two is quite straightforward:
a *Trigger* cannot alter the object that activated it, but it can do pretty much anything else.
...
To put it in SQL terms, EdgeDB's mutation rewrites correspond to SQL's `before` triggers, while EdgeDB's triggers align with SQL's
`after` triggers.

# Trigger: access to the full tuple supported? · Issue #5459 · edgedb/edgedb
created: 2023-05-10, last updated: 2024-12-13, [Read more](https://github.com/edgedb/edgedb/issues/5459)

Schema:
type Log {
required property body: json {}
abstract type Resource {
required property name: str {
rewrite insert, update using (str_trim(.name)); # NB: same behavior despite this rule
trigger _log_upsert_changes after insert, update for each do (
insert Log { body := <json>__new__ ++ <json>{ op := "upsert" } }
);
...
If you do select <json>Resource you'll get the same thing.
It jsonifies based on the shape.
You could try <json>(Resource {*}), though as a matter of style and architecture I'd maybe recommend enumerating the fields you actually want
select <json>Resource
...
This did the trick:
abstract type Resource {
trigger _do_log_upsert_changes after insert, update for each do (
insert Log { body := <json>(__new__ {*}) ++ <json>{ op := "upsert" } }
);
...
abstract type Auditable {
trigger _do_log_upsert_changes after insert, update for each do (
insert Log { new := <json>(__new__ {*}) ++ <json>{ op := "upsert" } }
);

